WEBVTT

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.303
Jeffrey, Belle,

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.135
we're going to be late
if we don't hurry.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.333
Come on, now.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.606
Line up next to the door,
children.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.578
Your father's ready
to leave for work.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.081
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.413
All right.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.974
Show me your fingernails.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.486
Very nicely done.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.317
Are your shoes polished?

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.481
Perfect.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.150
I'm very pleased, children,

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.159
and I'm sure
your father will be, too.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.990
I want to be first
to say good-bye to Daddy.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.324
Jeffrey always goes first.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.160
You were first yesterday.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.996
Now, children, little birds
in their nest get along.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.502
You're right, Mother.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.367
I'm sorry, Belle.
You can go first.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.202
No, it's really your turn.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.468
I did go first yesterday.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.476
Here he comes!

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.568
All right, now.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.375
Bright, happy faces.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.314
The coffee was quite good
this morning.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.317
I'm so glad you like it.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.343
I replicated a new blend
from Paksor III.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.184
I'll be home at the usual time.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.689
Now, don't let them
overwork you.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.352
You should save yourself
for the important things.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.792
Others can do the busywork.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.295
I couldn't agree more.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.796
I hope you have
a good day, Father.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.527
I'll have my homework finished
by the time you get back.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.194
I'll look forward
to reviewing it, Jeffrey.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.135
And is my little angel
going to get an "A"

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.297
on her history exam today?

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.669
Of course I will, Daddy.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.571
And can we do some algebra
problems when you get home?

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.973
Gladly.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.477
And don't forget...
you're going to ask

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.809
some of your friends from work
to have dinner with us.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.973
I'd like to meet them.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.413
I haven't forgotten.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.975
Well...

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.986
good-bye, all.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.352
Good-bye, Good-bye, Good-bye,
Daddy. Father. Darling.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.326
How's the new holofamily,
Doctor?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.022
They're everything
I could've hoped for.

00:03:31.643 --> 00:03:35.340
Captain's Log, Stardate 50836.2.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.314
We've had
long-range communications

00:03:37.348 --> 00:03:40.579
with a seemingly friendly race
known as the Vostigye.

00:03:40.618 --> 00:03:42.381
We'll be rendezvousing
within the hour

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.581
at one of their space stations.

00:03:44.622 --> 00:03:47.250
Ensign Kim, perhaps you could
direct your attention

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:49.817
to the sensors
and tell us if we're nearing

00:03:49.861 --> 00:03:51.624
the Vostigye space station.

00:03:51.663 --> 00:03:53.358
We should be getting close.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.797
That's funny.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.166
I'm not detecting it.

00:03:58.203 --> 00:03:59.932
You've checked the
coordinates they sent us?

00:03:59.971 --> 00:04:01.336
Yes, and...

00:04:01.372 --> 00:04:02.498
Hold on.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.338
Now I'm getting something.

00:04:05.376 --> 00:04:07.071
It's...

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.773
debris.

00:04:08.813 --> 00:04:09.939
Debris?!

00:04:10.014 --> 00:04:11.641
Confirmed.

00:04:11.683 --> 00:04:12.809
I am reading a debris field

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:14.512
encompassing
nearly 80 cubic kilometers.

00:04:14.552 --> 00:04:17.214
What's the composition
of the debris?

00:04:17.255 --> 00:04:20.622
Boronite, sarium,
carbon 60 composites.

00:04:20.658 --> 00:04:22.057
Sounds like it could've been
a space station.

00:04:22.093 --> 00:04:23.720
On screen.

00:04:28.066 --> 00:04:30.091
What happened to it?

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:32.660
Something ripped it apart.

00:04:32.704 --> 00:04:34.262
And from the energy
decay readings,

00:04:34.305 --> 00:04:36.136
I'd say it was no more
than an hour ago.

00:04:36.174 --> 00:04:37.573
I'm not picking up
any life signs, Captain.

00:04:37.609 --> 00:04:38.906
There don't appear to be
any survivors.

00:04:38.943 --> 00:04:43.642
There were 60 Vostigye
scientists on that station.

00:04:43.681 --> 00:04:45.911
I don't read any recognizable
weapon signatures.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.248
Maybe somebody in this part
of space has weapons

00:04:48.286 --> 00:04:50.277
that don't leave
a traditional signature.

00:04:50.321 --> 00:04:51.948
I'd like to know who they are,

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.424
and why they'd annihilate
a science station.

00:04:54.459 --> 00:04:55.926
Maybe we can find out,
Captain.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.689
There's a strange pattern

00:04:57.729 --> 00:04:59.959
that seems to be emanating
from subspace.

00:04:59.998 --> 00:05:02.262
Looks like some kind
of plasma particles.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.597
I've got it, too.

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:05.933
It's like a... a wake

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.733
leading away
from the debris field.

00:05:07.772 --> 00:05:09.330
From a ship?

00:05:09.374 --> 00:05:10.932
I can't tell.

00:05:10.975 --> 00:05:13.102
Set a course to follow it, Tom.

00:05:13.144 --> 00:05:15.544
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.741
Optical processors,
imaging array...

00:05:17.782 --> 00:05:19.545
they all check out, Doctor.

00:05:19.584 --> 00:05:21.211
You are in perfect health.

00:05:21.252 --> 00:05:22.617
I'm sure I could've
told you that.

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:23.780
Yes, I'm sure you could have,

00:05:23.822 --> 00:05:25.289
but with all the tinkering
you've been doing

00:05:25.323 --> 00:05:26.381
with your program lately,

00:05:26.424 --> 00:05:28.415
I'd feel better giving
you these little tune-ups

00:05:28.459 --> 00:05:29.619
on a regular basis.

00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:32.095
The tinkering you speak of
has been for the sole purpose

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.961
of improving my performance
as a physician.

00:05:34.032 --> 00:05:35.431
I can hardly
be faulted for that.

00:05:35.466 --> 00:05:37.263
I'm not faulting you
for your intentions, Doctor.

00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:38.599
I think it's rather commendable

00:05:38.636 --> 00:05:40.126
that you want
to improve yourself.

00:05:40.171 --> 00:05:42.731
That's why I've created
a family.

00:05:42.774 --> 00:05:44.469
A family?

00:05:44.509 --> 00:05:45.737
I've listened
to enough patients

00:05:45.777 --> 00:05:47.244
talk about their families
to realize

00:05:47.278 --> 00:05:49.610
how meaningful they are
to biological beings.

00:05:49.647 --> 00:05:51.444
For better or worse, yes.

00:05:51.482 --> 00:05:52.506
The Doctor has created

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:53.812
a holographic wife
and two children,

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:56.286
so that he can experience
family life for himself.

00:05:56.321 --> 00:05:57.618
Interesting.

00:05:57.655 --> 00:05:59.953
And how's it going so far?

00:05:59.991 --> 00:06:01.458
Splendidly.
From what I heard,

00:06:01.492 --> 00:06:03.119
I thought it would be difficult,

00:06:03.161 --> 00:06:04.822
but I'm enjoying the experience.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.490
You are?

00:06:06.531 --> 00:06:09.659
Funny. I never thought of you
as a family man, Doc.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.498
I'd like to meet them.

00:06:11.536 --> 00:06:13.197
As a matter of fact,

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:14.830
the "little woman" has
been asking me to bring

00:06:14.873 --> 00:06:16.238
some of my colleagues
home for dinner.

00:06:16.274 --> 00:06:19.801
Perhaps you and Kes
would care to join us tonight?

00:06:19.844 --> 00:06:21.903
Charlene is a wonderful cook.

00:06:21.946 --> 00:06:23.937
I'd like to meet them, too.

00:06:24.048 --> 00:06:28.075
Well, Doc, tell your wife
to haul out the good china.

00:06:28.119 --> 00:06:30.178
You're having company.

00:06:33.291 --> 00:06:35.122
Ah.

00:06:35.159 --> 00:06:38.925
Please, have some more
wild mushroom pilaf, B'Elanna.

00:06:38.963 --> 00:06:41.431
Uh, thanks. I've had
two helpings already.

00:06:41.466 --> 00:06:42.763
It's delicious.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.769
I took a course
in continental cuisine

00:06:45.803 --> 00:06:48.795
so I could replicate
interesting meals

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.364
for Kenneth.

00:06:50.408 --> 00:06:51.375
Kenneth?

00:06:51.409 --> 00:06:52.535
My husband.

00:06:52.577 --> 00:06:54.306
What do you call him?

00:06:54.345 --> 00:06:56.677
Oh, we call him Doctor.

00:06:56.714 --> 00:06:57.976
Oh, of course.

00:06:58.049 --> 00:06:59.778
Anyway, he works terribly hard

00:06:59.817 --> 00:07:02.377
and he's under
such great stress.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.547
I want this home
to be his sanctuary,

00:07:04.589 --> 00:07:07.524
the place he can come

00:07:07.558 --> 00:07:10.322
and have all the cares
of the day disappear.

00:07:10.361 --> 00:07:12.022
How nice for him.

00:07:12.063 --> 00:07:13.826
My daddy is
a very important man.

00:07:13.865 --> 00:07:15.730
He's the best doctor
there ever was,

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:17.928
and he saves people's lives
all the time.

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:19.333
A slight exaggeration.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.496
It is not!
You said...

00:07:20.538 --> 00:07:21.937
Belle, eat your dinner.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.065
They're well aware
of my talents.

00:07:24.108 --> 00:07:25.735
Jeffrey, why don't
you tell our guests

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:27.210
about your new project
at school.

00:07:27.245 --> 00:07:29.679
I've designed
a micro-filter implant

00:07:29.714 --> 00:07:30.874
which will make it possible

00:07:30.915 --> 00:07:32.712
to cleanse blood
of harmful microorganisms

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.184
too small to stimulate
an immune response.

00:07:35.219 --> 00:07:36.777
Jeffrey is extremely bright.

00:07:36.821 --> 00:07:38.914
He's in the accelerated
physical sciences

00:07:38.957 --> 00:07:39.946
program at school.

00:07:40.024 --> 00:07:43.187
A regular chip
off the old block, right?

00:07:43.227 --> 00:07:44.922
And don't forget
about our little Belle.

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:45.930
She's already

00:07:45.964 --> 00:07:47.727
studying algebra
and trigonometry

00:07:47.765 --> 00:07:50.734
and she's quite
the budding athlete.

00:07:50.768 --> 00:07:52.668
You must be very proud
of your family, Doctor.

00:07:52.704 --> 00:07:53.966
Oh...

00:07:54.038 --> 00:07:56.165
Well, we're proud of him, too.

00:07:56.207 --> 00:08:00.166
In fact, we think we have
just about the most wonderful

00:08:00.211 --> 00:08:02.839
husband and father
in the Quadrant, don't we?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.211
Computer, freeze program.

00:08:04.248 --> 00:08:05.715
Yes, we d...

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.843
Lieutenant, what are you doing?

00:08:07.885 --> 00:08:10.877
I am stopping this before
my blood sugar levels overload.

00:08:10.922 --> 00:08:12.549
Doctor...

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:13.887
Yes?

00:08:13.925 --> 00:08:15.324
If you think
that this is giving you

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.920
an accurate impression
of being in a family,

00:08:17.962 --> 00:08:19.589
you are sadly mistaken.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:20.688
I don't understand.

00:08:20.732 --> 00:08:22.063
They're kind of perfect.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.692
They are ridiculously perfect.

00:08:23.735 --> 00:08:25.430
No one has a family like this.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.869
This is a fantasy.

00:08:26.904 --> 00:08:28.428
You're not going
to learn anything

00:08:28.473 --> 00:08:31.465
from being with these...
Iollipops.

00:08:31.509 --> 00:08:32.669
I provided the computer

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:35.042
with my requirements
for a mate and children.

00:08:35.079 --> 00:08:37.912
If I were to choose a real wife,
my taste would be the same...

00:08:37.949 --> 00:08:39.940
intelligence, education,
organizational skills...

00:08:40.051 --> 00:08:42.383
There is nothing wrong
with your premise, Doctor.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:46.652
It just needs a little tweaking
to bring it closer to real life.

00:08:48.159 --> 00:08:50.218
I can help...

00:08:51.195 --> 00:08:52.958
if you'd like.

00:08:58.336 --> 00:09:00.634
Captain, the particle wake
we've been following

00:09:00.671 --> 00:09:01.729
is beginning to thin out.

00:09:01.773 --> 00:09:04.606
Is there any indication
what caused it?

00:09:04.642 --> 00:09:06.837
I am detecting no ships,
no structures,

00:09:06.878 --> 00:09:08.436
no weapon signatures.

00:09:08.479 --> 00:09:09.411
Wait a minute.

00:09:09.447 --> 00:09:10.846
Something.

00:09:10.882 --> 00:09:12.349
I see it, too.

00:09:12.383 --> 00:09:13.645
A subspace disruption.

00:09:13.684 --> 00:09:15.208
What's causing it?

00:09:15.253 --> 00:09:17.813
I can't tell, but it's
getting more intense.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.617
Shields up.
Red Alert.

00:09:22.827 --> 00:09:24.294
Tom, back us off.

00:09:25.663 --> 00:09:27.358
Something's coming out
of subspace.

00:09:38.876 --> 00:09:40.741
Tom, move us away!

00:09:40.778 --> 00:09:41.802
I don't have engines!

00:09:41.846 --> 00:09:42.835
Propulsion is off-line.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:43.938
So is navigational control.

00:09:44.015 --> 00:09:46.506
Bridge to Engineering.
We need power.

00:09:46.551 --> 00:09:47.813
I'm on it, Captain.

00:09:47.852 --> 00:09:51.618
The anomaly is bearing down
on us, heading 047 mark 19.

00:09:51.656 --> 00:09:53.624
Brace for impact.

00:09:57.562 --> 00:09:59.462
It hit our starboard shields.

00:09:59.497 --> 00:10:00.930
There's damage on Deck 3.

00:10:00.965 --> 00:10:03.263
Ready weapons.
We're going to disperse it.

00:10:03.301 --> 00:10:04.666
Phasers on line...

00:10:04.702 --> 00:10:06.636
Wait a minute.

00:10:16.547 --> 00:10:18.481
I'm not afraid to say it.

00:10:18.516 --> 00:10:20.484
I've never seen anything
like that before.

00:10:20.518 --> 00:10:22.383
Damage report.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:25.150
20 percent loss of the
starboard dorsal shields

00:10:25.189 --> 00:10:27.180
and minor buckling
of the hull on Deck 3.

00:10:27.225 --> 00:10:28.419
No indication of casualties.

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:30.586
We've got propulsion
systems back on line.

00:10:30.628 --> 00:10:32.459
I think I can put
some distance between us

00:10:32.497 --> 00:10:33.486
and whatever that was.

00:10:33.531 --> 00:10:35.795
Maybe we don't want to.

00:10:35.833 --> 00:10:37.892
We've just witnessed
a phenomenon

00:10:37.935 --> 00:10:39.664
none of us
has ever heard of before,

00:10:39.704 --> 00:10:41.171
much less experienced.

00:10:41.205 --> 00:10:42.263
On a purely scientific level,

00:10:42.306 --> 00:10:46.003
I think we owe it to ourselves
to investigate.

00:10:46.077 --> 00:10:47.977
I'm looking at the telemetry
we collected.

00:10:48.012 --> 00:10:50.845
It was an astral eddy
that seems to have formed

00:10:50.882 --> 00:10:53.112
at the confluence
of space and subspace.

00:10:53.151 --> 00:10:54.618
It was highly charged
with plasma.

00:10:54.652 --> 00:10:55.846
That explains the particle wake.

00:10:55.887 --> 00:10:57.821
If we could harness
some of that energy,

00:10:57.855 --> 00:10:59.846
we could go off replicator
rations for a while.

00:10:59.891 --> 00:11:02.553
Captain, we don't have any idea
what caused that phenomenon

00:11:02.593 --> 00:11:04.288
or what made it dissipate.

00:11:04.328 --> 00:11:05.852
So how do we investigate it
if it's gone?

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:08.058
I suspect there are conditions
in this part of space

00:11:08.099 --> 00:11:10.727
that lend themselves to the
formation of those eddies.

00:11:10.768 --> 00:11:14.704
Set sensors for continuous scans
of subspace.

00:11:14.739 --> 00:11:17.230
Maybe we can anticipate
the next one.

00:11:24.248 --> 00:11:26.978
I thought for a long time about
what Lieutenant Torres said

00:11:27.084 --> 00:11:28.984
and I finally concluded
she was right.

00:11:29.053 --> 00:11:31.283
If I'm going to have
the experience of a family,

00:11:31.322 --> 00:11:32.983
it should be
as authentic as possible.

00:11:33.024 --> 00:11:34.992
What changes have you asked her
to make in the program?

00:11:35.092 --> 00:11:36.354
Oh, she's already made them.

00:11:36.394 --> 00:11:37.827
She simply added some randomized

00:11:37.862 --> 00:11:40.194
behavioral algorithms
to the program I constructed.

00:11:40.231 --> 00:11:42.165
How will that
affect your family?

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.690
Events will simply unfold

00:11:43.734 --> 00:11:45.759
as a natural evolution
of probabilities

00:11:45.803 --> 00:11:47.134
within the program.

00:11:47.171 --> 00:11:48.934
But there's no way to predict
what those might be.

00:11:48.973 --> 00:11:50.338
That could mean a few surprises.

00:11:50.374 --> 00:11:51.932
Are you sure you're
ready for this?

00:11:51.976 --> 00:11:54.001
My database contains
everything there is to know

00:11:54.045 --> 00:11:56.946
about pediatric care
and childhood development.

00:11:56.981 --> 00:11:59.347
I can't imagine a parenting
problem I couldn't handle.

00:11:59.383 --> 00:12:01.351
Your wife will have changed,
too.

00:12:02.553 --> 00:12:07.149
Well, I have had some experience
with romantic relationships.

00:12:07.191 --> 00:12:09.182
I don't anticipate
any problems there.

00:12:09.227 --> 00:12:10.626
Sounds like you have
it all worked out.

00:12:10.661 --> 00:12:12.891
When do you plan on meeting
this new, improved family?

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:13.954
Right now.

00:12:13.998 --> 00:12:15.226
I'm due home for dinner.

00:12:15.266 --> 00:12:16.233
Computer,

00:12:16.267 --> 00:12:18.497
initiate Doctor's
family program Beta-Rho

00:12:18.536 --> 00:12:20.902
and transfer the EMH
to Holodeck 2.

00:12:23.574 --> 00:12:24.700
Hello!

00:12:24.742 --> 00:12:26.232
I'm...

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.707
home.

00:12:30.748 --> 00:12:32.375
There you are.

00:12:32.416 --> 00:12:33.974
I thought you'd never get here.

00:12:34.051 --> 00:12:35.518
It was a busy day.

00:12:35.553 --> 00:12:38.283
I was quite challenged
by the task of preparing

00:12:38.322 --> 00:12:41.450
a DNA probe to test Ensign
Parson's glial cells.

00:12:41.492 --> 00:12:44.928
It seems he has
a microbial infection.

00:12:44.962 --> 00:12:45.929
Rather unusual.

00:12:45.963 --> 00:12:47.225
Tell me about it
when I get home.

00:12:47.265 --> 00:12:48.232
I'm late already.

00:12:48.266 --> 00:12:49.233
Late?

00:12:49.267 --> 00:12:50.666
Oh... it's Wednesday, remember?

00:12:50.701 --> 00:12:52.464
I'm speaking
at the Bolian Embassy.

00:12:52.503 --> 00:12:53.993
Ah, right.

00:12:54.071 --> 00:12:55.197
Is dinner ready?

00:12:55.239 --> 00:12:57.002
It's your night to cook.

00:12:57.108 --> 00:12:59.008
Mom, I can't find my ion mallet!

00:12:59.076 --> 00:13:02.375
If you cleaned your room,
you'd have better luck!

00:13:03.714 --> 00:13:05.113
What is that noise?

00:13:05.149 --> 00:13:07.208
Oh... I've had
to listen to it all day.

00:13:07.251 --> 00:13:09.014
Maybe you can do
something about it.

00:13:10.021 --> 00:13:11.579
Daddy!
You've got to help me!

00:13:11.622 --> 00:13:13.180
I'll be late for practice.

00:13:13.224 --> 00:13:14.919
Coach Morgan will be furious
if I'm late again.

00:13:14.959 --> 00:13:16.950
If you put your mallet
in your closet

00:13:16.994 --> 00:13:19.189
when you were done with it,
you'd know where it was.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.527
I know that, Daddy!

00:13:20.564 --> 00:13:22.862
Oh!
Tell Jeffrey to turn that off!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:23.958
It makes my eyes hurt!

00:13:24.068 --> 00:13:24.966
Mine, too.

00:13:25.069 --> 00:13:27.697
Jeffrey! Jeffrey!

00:13:27.738 --> 00:13:29.706
What?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.765
What is that music?

00:13:31.809 --> 00:13:33.367
Klingon.

00:13:33.411 --> 00:13:34.969
Well, turn it down!
You can't do your homework

00:13:35.079 --> 00:13:36.546
with that noise.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.138
- Daddy, I can't find my mallet!
- I know that, Belle.

00:13:38.182 --> 00:13:39.672
The coach will send me
down to the second team!

00:13:39.717 --> 00:13:41.548
Well, perhaps that will
teach you a lesson.

00:13:41.585 --> 00:13:42.574
You don't understand anything!

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:43.587
Belle, you have to realize...

00:13:48.926 --> 00:13:50.484
Where's Jeffrey?

00:13:50.528 --> 00:13:51.552
Who are you?

00:13:51.595 --> 00:13:52.892
Friends.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.830
Do you have names?

00:13:54.865 --> 00:13:55.991
Larg.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.362
K'Kath.

00:13:57.401 --> 00:14:00.700
Well, Larg, K'Kath,
you'll have to come back later.

00:14:00.738 --> 00:14:01.830
Jeffrey's doing his homework.

00:14:01.872 --> 00:14:02.839
He invited us.

00:14:02.873 --> 00:14:05.671
Daddy! I need my ion mallet!

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.699
I!

00:14:07.712 --> 00:14:09.407
Just a minute.

00:14:09.447 --> 00:14:10.846
I'm sorry, but Jeffrey
can't see friends

00:14:10.881 --> 00:14:12.678
until he has finished
his homework.

00:14:12.717 --> 00:14:15.652
Dad... I asked them to come.

00:14:15.686 --> 00:14:16.948
Daddy!

00:14:16.987 --> 00:14:18.147
Jeffrey, this is unacceptable.

00:14:18.189 --> 00:14:19.656
It'll only take a minute.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.385
We have some business
we have to do.

00:14:21.425 --> 00:14:23.188
Business?

00:14:23.227 --> 00:14:24.489
YigHoS pa'wijdaQ.

00:14:24.528 --> 00:14:25.552
Qay'be'.

00:14:25.596 --> 00:14:26.654
Where's my mallet?
I need it now!

00:14:26.697 --> 00:14:27.664
Young man!

00:14:27.698 --> 00:14:28.665
You're mean!

00:14:28.699 --> 00:14:30.667
You don't love me as much
as Mommy does.

00:14:30.701 --> 00:14:32.002
She'd help me find my mallet!

00:14:32.135 --> 00:14:33.966
I want Mommy! I want Mommy!

00:14:34.037 --> 00:14:35.402
I want Mommy!
I want Mommy!

00:14:49.052 --> 00:14:51.111
Nothing striking your fancy,
Lieutenant?

00:14:51.154 --> 00:14:52.678
Isn't this the fourth
day in a row,

00:14:52.722 --> 00:14:53.916
we've had the same casserole?

00:14:55.258 --> 00:14:57.624
Pleeka rinds and grub meal...

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.992
very tasty,
if I do say so myself.

00:15:00.063 --> 00:15:02.793
Well, you did a great job
with it, no question.

00:15:02.832 --> 00:15:04.800
It'd just be nice
to have a little variety.

00:15:04.834 --> 00:15:07.769
Well, you're perfectly free
to use the replicators.

00:15:07.804 --> 00:15:10.773
Um, I'm out of rations.

00:15:12.642 --> 00:15:13.734
Then...

00:15:17.747 --> 00:15:19.374
enjoy the casserole.

00:15:29.292 --> 00:15:32.489
A beautiful woman should
never have to eat alone.

00:15:32.529 --> 00:15:34.326
What are you reading?

00:15:34.364 --> 00:15:35.797
It's nothing important.

00:15:40.236 --> 00:15:43.763
Women Warriors
at the River of Blood?

00:15:43.807 --> 00:15:46.674
It's just... escapist reading.

00:15:48.278 --> 00:15:51.145
"Rorg turned his fierce eye
upon her

00:15:51.181 --> 00:15:53.081
"and M'Nea felt her heart
begin to quicken

00:15:53.116 --> 00:15:55.744
"even as her hand
went to her dagger.

00:15:55.785 --> 00:15:57.980
"She had intended to plunge it
into his throat,

00:15:58.088 --> 00:16:01.114
but something about him
made her hesitate."

00:16:01.157 --> 00:16:04.820
B'Elanna, is this
a Klingon romance novel?

00:16:04.861 --> 00:16:08.558
Klingons do have what you
might call a romantic side.

00:16:08.598 --> 00:16:11.328
It's a bit more vigorous
than most.

00:16:12.902 --> 00:16:15.063
I think I'll read it.

00:16:15.105 --> 00:16:16.697
Maybe it'll give me some ideas

00:16:16.739 --> 00:16:18.730
about how
to make your heart quicken.

00:16:18.775 --> 00:16:20.743
It's not a technical manual,
Tom.

00:16:20.777 --> 00:16:23.371
Well, that depends on what
you mean by "technical."

00:16:23.413 --> 00:16:25.881
To an engineer, that means...

00:16:25.915 --> 00:16:29.612
"specializing
in particular systems."

00:16:29.652 --> 00:16:31.847
I think that definition works.

00:16:31.888 --> 00:16:34.584
Well, I can't promise I won't
put a dagger in your throat.

00:16:35.758 --> 00:16:37.783
Have you heard
about the Doctor's new family?

00:16:39.329 --> 00:16:40.421
How's it going?

00:16:40.463 --> 00:16:42.590
I think he was a little
overwhelmed at first,

00:16:42.632 --> 00:16:44.566
but I have to give him credit.

00:16:44.601 --> 00:16:46.091
He's sticking with it.

00:16:46.136 --> 00:16:49.594
It's hard to imagine
the Doctor with children.

00:16:58.314 --> 00:17:01.215
Senior staff to the Bridge
immediately.

00:17:11.861 --> 00:17:14.489
Tom, I want to send a probe
into that anomaly.

00:17:14.531 --> 00:17:15.725
Can you hold position
close enough

00:17:15.765 --> 00:17:17.494
for us to get
accurate telemetry?

00:17:17.534 --> 00:17:18.762
I can try.

00:17:18.801 --> 00:17:22.293
Be ready to move away quickly
if it starts moving toward us.

00:17:23.306 --> 00:17:24.273
Sorry about that.

00:17:24.307 --> 00:17:25.331
Just trying

00:17:25.375 --> 00:17:26.842
to find a way to ride
the graviton waves

00:17:26.876 --> 00:17:27.934
it's throwing off.

00:17:31.414 --> 00:17:33.780
There.
That's a little better.

00:17:35.418 --> 00:17:37.784
We're in as good a position
as we're going to be.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:38.752
Tuvok?

00:17:38.788 --> 00:17:40.585
The probe has been launched.

00:17:46.529 --> 00:17:48.497
Actually, this is kind of fun.

00:17:49.465 --> 00:17:50.796
Speak for yourself.

00:17:50.833 --> 00:17:52.960
We're starting
to receive telemetry.

00:17:53.002 --> 00:17:55.766
Captain, this is
one weird disturbance.

00:17:55.805 --> 00:17:57.534
I'm reading
a temperature gradient

00:17:57.574 --> 00:17:58.871
of nine million kelvins,

00:17:58.908 --> 00:18:01.240
massive discharges
of plasmatic energy

00:18:01.277 --> 00:18:03.006
and there's a perfectly calm eye
at the center.

00:18:03.046 --> 00:18:04.479
Apparently, some of the matter

00:18:04.514 --> 00:18:08.006
inside it is being exchanged
between space and subspace.

00:18:08.051 --> 00:18:09.348
What about the plasma?

00:18:09.385 --> 00:18:11.512
Is there any way we can transfer
some of it to Voyager?

00:18:11.554 --> 00:18:12.578
I don't see how.

00:18:12.622 --> 00:18:14.613
We can't transport
with this kind of turbulence.

00:18:14.657 --> 00:18:16.591
Maybe we could try a...

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:22.491
We lost it.

00:18:22.532 --> 00:18:23.863
Where's the probe?

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.231
It's disappeared.

00:18:25.268 --> 00:18:26.394
It's still transmitting,

00:18:26.436 --> 00:18:27.733
but there's a lot
of interference.

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:31.467
I'm detecting some kind
of unstable interfold layer,

00:18:31.507 --> 00:18:33.475
not in space or subspace.

00:18:33.509 --> 00:18:35.238
It could be where
the eddies originate

00:18:35.278 --> 00:18:36.575
and where the probe is now.

00:18:36.613 --> 00:18:37.739
We've got another particle wake.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:39.543
Since we can't get
plasma directly

00:18:39.582 --> 00:18:42.676
from the eddies, maybe we could
collect some from their wakes.

00:18:42.719 --> 00:18:44.482
The Bussard collectors
could be modified

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.317
to gather plasma particles.

00:18:46.356 --> 00:18:47.448
We could do that,

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.151
but Voyager's energy
emissions are so high,

00:18:49.192 --> 00:18:50.716
they'd corrupt the particles.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.955
I'm not sure the plasma
would be much use to us.

00:18:52.996 --> 00:18:54.224
What if I took a shuttle out?

00:18:54.264 --> 00:18:55.754
The energy emissions
would be a lot lower.

00:18:55.798 --> 00:18:57.891
That sounds like
it's worth a try.

00:18:57.934 --> 00:19:00.596
Well, you'd be exposing yourself
to radiation poisoning.

00:19:00.637 --> 00:19:01.569
Check with the Doctor.

00:19:01.604 --> 00:19:03.128
Maybe he can give you
some kind of protection.

00:19:03.172 --> 00:19:04.230
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:04.274 --> 00:19:05.935
I'll head to the shuttle bay
as soon as I'm done.

00:19:12.448 --> 00:19:15.178
I've given you a combination
of hyronalin and lectrazine.

00:19:15.218 --> 00:19:16.913
That should give you
temporary protection.

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.612
But I can't guarantee
its duration.

00:19:18.655 --> 00:19:19.849
That's all right, Doc.

00:19:19.889 --> 00:19:21.686
I don't think I'll be
out there too long.

00:19:21.724 --> 00:19:24.284
If I know you, you'll
push it to the limit.

00:19:24.327 --> 00:19:25.919
You enjoy flirting with danger.

00:19:26.029 --> 00:19:27.257
You know me too well.

00:19:27.297 --> 00:19:28.787
You were undoubtedly
one of those children

00:19:28.831 --> 00:19:30.856
who had to climb
the highest tree...

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:32.765
scale the tallest cliff.

00:19:32.802 --> 00:19:34.360
That was me.

00:19:34.404 --> 00:19:35.371
I can only imagine

00:19:35.405 --> 00:19:37.066
what you must have put
your parents through.

00:19:38.241 --> 00:19:40.300
How's the family, Doc?

00:19:40.343 --> 00:19:42.573
I hear they're a real handful.

00:19:42.612 --> 00:19:45.479
Indeed. However, I have
analyzed the situation

00:19:45.515 --> 00:19:46.743
and come up with a solution.

00:19:46.783 --> 00:19:48.580
There should be
no more problems.

00:19:48.618 --> 00:19:52.054
You make it sound like
you're treating a sick patient.

00:19:52.088 --> 00:19:55.489
I'm not sure you can
diagnose and cure a family.

00:19:55.525 --> 00:19:56.958
We'll see.

00:19:57.026 --> 00:19:58.960
You're in fine physical
shape, Lieutenant.

00:19:59.062 --> 00:20:01.656
You may go ahead and engage
in this reckless activity.

00:20:01.698 --> 00:20:03.893
Thanks, Doc.

00:20:10.807 --> 00:20:12.297
Where's Jeffrey?!

00:20:12.342 --> 00:20:13.934
He's coming.

00:20:13.976 --> 00:20:17.104
I asked everyone to be here
at 1600 hours, precisely.

00:20:17.146 --> 00:20:18.636
Jeffrey was asleep.

00:20:18.681 --> 00:20:21.844
Asleep?
In the middle of the afternoon?

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:26.284
Is this true?
Were you asleep?

00:20:26.322 --> 00:20:27.482
Are you sick?

00:20:27.523 --> 00:20:30.424
I had a late night.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:32.428
That's one of the matters
I want to discuss.

00:20:32.462 --> 00:20:34.453
Thank you all for coming.

00:20:34.497 --> 00:20:36.124
I thought it would be
a good idea

00:20:36.165 --> 00:20:37.564
if we had a family meeting.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:40.330
In fact, I'd like to do this
on a regular basis.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:42.668
That's something
to look forward to.

00:20:42.705 --> 00:20:44.002
If you have something
to say, Jeffrey,

00:20:44.107 --> 00:20:46.302
say it so everyone can hear.

00:20:46.342 --> 00:20:48.037
Nothing.

00:20:50.947 --> 00:20:53.006
I've been feeling
that this family

00:20:53.049 --> 00:20:55.244
is beginning to spin
out of control.

00:20:55.284 --> 00:20:56.342
As husband and father,

00:20:56.386 --> 00:20:59.480
I believe it is my duty
to set some parameters.

00:20:59.522 --> 00:21:01.353
It's part of good parenting.

00:21:01.391 --> 00:21:03.052
What are parameters?

00:21:03.092 --> 00:21:05.219
Limits. Boundaries.

00:21:05.261 --> 00:21:08.560
To that end, I have drawn up

00:21:08.598 --> 00:21:11.726
a revised family schedule and
a list of rules and regulations.

00:21:11.768 --> 00:21:14.134
I'd like you all
to study them carefully.

00:21:15.271 --> 00:21:17.899
You've rearranged
my lecture nights!

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:19.635
I had to do that in order
to make everything work.

00:21:19.675 --> 00:21:22.473
Everybody has had
to make some sacrifices.

00:21:22.512 --> 00:21:23.979
Daddy!
You changed parrises' squares

00:21:24.046 --> 00:21:26.310
from Monday-Wednesday-Friday
to Tuesday-Thursday-Saturday!

00:21:26.349 --> 00:21:27.577
- Mm-hmm.
- That puts me

00:21:27.617 --> 00:21:28.584
on the second team!

00:21:28.618 --> 00:21:29.983
I'm good enough to be
on the first team!

00:21:30.019 --> 00:21:31.384
You shouldn't be
on the first team.

00:21:31.421 --> 00:21:32.786
You're not old enough.

00:21:32.822 --> 00:21:35.985
As I said, Belle,
we must all make sacrifices.

00:21:36.092 --> 00:21:38.083
What sacrifices did you make?

00:21:39.395 --> 00:21:42.853
I will make dinner on the nights
your mother lectures.

00:21:42.899 --> 00:21:44.890
You do that anyway.
That's not a sacrifice.

00:21:45.902 --> 00:21:48.837
What's this mean
about no Klingon friends?!

00:21:48.871 --> 00:21:49.997
Exactly that.

00:21:50.039 --> 00:21:51.768
They're a bad influence on you.

00:21:51.808 --> 00:21:53.742
They're prone to violence,
they keep you out

00:21:53.776 --> 00:21:55.004
till all hours.

00:21:55.111 --> 00:21:57.579
Why don't you find
some nice Vulcan friends?

00:21:57.613 --> 00:22:00.013
You can't just decide
who my friends will be!

00:22:00.116 --> 00:22:01.014
Hold on.

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:03.951
Kenneth, that may be
a bit unreasonable.

00:22:04.887 --> 00:22:06.252
Charlene?

00:22:15.298 --> 00:22:16.492
You know very well

00:22:16.532 --> 00:22:19.194
how important it is
to keep a united front.

00:22:19.235 --> 00:22:22.227
I expect you to support
me in these decisions.

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.603
Well, if that's what you expect

00:22:25.641 --> 00:22:27.700
then maybe you should have
asked my opinion

00:22:27.743 --> 00:22:30.109
before you started
unilaterally deciding things.

00:22:30.146 --> 00:22:32.671
I'm not one of the children,
after all.

00:22:32.715 --> 00:22:34.444
I believe I should
have some say

00:22:34.484 --> 00:22:37.976
in just what rules and
regulations are established!

00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:40.420
And I think it's unfair
for you to tell Jeffrey

00:22:40.456 --> 00:22:42.754
what friends he can
and cannot have.

00:22:42.792 --> 00:22:45.761
Right! This whole meeting
is a vulky idea!

00:22:45.795 --> 00:22:47.626
And you can have it without me.

00:22:47.663 --> 00:22:48.891
Jeffrey, you were not excused!

00:22:48.931 --> 00:22:50.865
You've upset him.
Let him go.

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:52.993
I don't want to argue this
in front of the children.

00:22:53.069 --> 00:22:54.764
We'll discuss it later.

00:23:01.644 --> 00:23:04.613
You really made a mess of
things, didn't you, Daddy?

00:23:04.647 --> 00:23:07.616
Apparently so.

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:11.643
Although, I must admit, I fail
to understand the reaction.

00:23:11.687 --> 00:23:14.622
I... I'm just trying

00:23:14.657 --> 00:23:17.820
to help the family
function better.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.760
How does it make the family
function better

00:23:19.795 --> 00:23:22.923
if I go to parrises' squares
Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday?

00:23:22.965 --> 00:23:25.559
Belle, you've been playing
with children

00:23:25.601 --> 00:23:27.432
two and three years older
than you.

00:23:27.470 --> 00:23:28.960
That's much too dangerous.

00:23:29.038 --> 00:23:30.938
But that's what's fun about it.

00:23:33.142 --> 00:23:35.906
You're not old enough
to realize

00:23:35.945 --> 00:23:38.277
how hazardous that game can be.

00:23:38.314 --> 00:23:40.248
It's up to me to keep you safe.

00:23:40.283 --> 00:23:42.114
I...

00:23:42.151 --> 00:23:44.415
I'm just trying
to be a good father.

00:23:52.995 --> 00:23:57.295
If it'll help, Daddy,
I'll be on the second team.

00:23:59.168 --> 00:24:00.931
Thank you, Belle.

00:24:00.970 --> 00:24:02.938
That's very grown-up of you.

00:24:03.005 --> 00:24:05.872
And I think you're
a very good father.

00:24:07.944 --> 00:24:11.402
Why... thank you.

00:24:12.782 --> 00:24:14.875
I love you, Daddy...

00:24:14.917 --> 00:24:18.318
even if you did
make a mess of things.

00:24:29.632 --> 00:24:31.099
Voyager to
Shuttlecraft Cochrane.

00:24:31.133 --> 00:24:32.100
Do you read?

00:24:32.134 --> 00:24:33.396
Loud and clear, Captain.

00:24:33.436 --> 00:24:35.961
I'm about 3,000 kilometers
from the eddy.

00:24:36.038 --> 00:24:39.098
As soon as it dissipates,
I'll head for the particle wake.

00:24:39.141 --> 00:24:40.802
If this one follows
the pattern of the others,

00:24:40.843 --> 00:24:43.175
it should begin to collapse
within a few seconds.

00:24:43.212 --> 00:24:44.201
That's good.

00:24:44.246 --> 00:24:45.508
I'm beginning to wish
I hadn't had

00:24:45.548 --> 00:24:47.982
that second helping
of French toast this morning.

00:24:48.084 --> 00:24:49.779
Captain.

00:24:49.819 --> 00:24:51.343
The eddy
is starting to dissipate.

00:24:51.387 --> 00:24:52.445
Stand by, Tom.

00:24:52.488 --> 00:24:53.716
I'm ready.

00:24:58.394 --> 00:24:59.986
I'm in position, Captain.

00:25:00.029 --> 00:25:02.190
Activating
the Bussard collectors.

00:25:03.599 --> 00:25:05.089
It's working.

00:25:05.134 --> 00:25:07.227
This may save us from Neelix's

00:25:07.269 --> 00:25:08.930
pleeka rind casserole
after all.

00:25:09.005 --> 00:25:11.439
We'll all thank you for that.

00:25:11.474 --> 00:25:12.441
Captain.

00:25:12.475 --> 00:25:14.102
Subspace disruption.

00:25:14.143 --> 00:25:15.440
Is another eddy forming?

00:25:15.478 --> 00:25:16.809
It looks that way.

00:25:16.846 --> 00:25:18.108
Tom, get out of there...

00:25:18.147 --> 00:25:19.114
now.

00:25:19.148 --> 00:25:20.137
I'm going.

00:25:27.023 --> 00:25:28.388
Harry, can you beam him out?

00:25:28.424 --> 00:25:30.221
Transporters are off line.

00:25:30.259 --> 00:25:31.487
I'm working on them.

00:25:31.527 --> 00:25:33.294
Tom, are you there?

00:25:33.427 --> 00:25:34.325
It's pulling me in!

00:25:34.361 --> 00:25:36.955
I don't have enough power!

00:25:37.031 --> 00:25:38.430
Where are the transporters?

00:25:38.465 --> 00:25:39.955
I can't access them!

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:41.331
The shuttle's being drawn
inside the eddy.

00:25:41.368 --> 00:25:43.802
Janeway to Paris.
Do you read me?

00:25:43.837 --> 00:25:44.826
Captain...

00:25:44.872 --> 00:25:46.897
the astral eddy
is beginning to dissipate.

00:26:01.955 --> 00:26:03.217
Harry, when the probe
disappeared,

00:26:03.257 --> 00:26:04.224
it kept transmitting.

00:26:04.258 --> 00:26:05.225
What about Tom's shuttle?

00:26:05.259 --> 00:26:07.022
We're getting
a lot interference.

00:26:07.061 --> 00:26:08.551
I can't tell if it's
a transmission or not.

00:26:08.595 --> 00:26:10.358
See if you can clean it up.

00:26:12.399 --> 00:26:14.162
I've adjusted
the encoding filter.

00:26:14.201 --> 00:26:15.168
Try it now.

00:26:15.202 --> 00:26:16.499
Voyager to Tom Paris.

00:26:16.537 --> 00:26:17.834
Can you hear us?

00:26:17.871 --> 00:26:18.860
Respond.

00:26:21.275 --> 00:26:22.936
Calibrate
to a theta-band frequency.

00:26:22.976 --> 00:26:24.944
Maybe that'll help.

00:26:25.012 --> 00:26:26.240
I can't hear you, Captain.

00:26:26.280 --> 00:26:28.271
There's a lot
of plasma interference.

00:26:28.315 --> 00:26:29.441
I can't clean it up.

00:26:29.483 --> 00:26:31.417
Say again, Tom.
You're breaking up.

00:26:31.452 --> 00:26:33.716
Adjust your transceiver
lock and try again.

00:26:33.754 --> 00:26:37.087
I can hear you.
Is that better?

00:26:37.124 --> 00:26:38.489
Yes, a little.

00:26:38.525 --> 00:26:39.924
Where are you?

00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:42.053
Captain,
I wish I could tell you.

00:27:19.333 --> 00:27:20.300
Doctor?

00:27:20.334 --> 00:27:21.301
Hmm?

00:27:21.335 --> 00:27:22.700
Can I help you with something?

00:27:22.736 --> 00:27:23.930
Oh, no, no.

00:27:23.971 --> 00:27:26.064
Perhaps.

00:27:26.106 --> 00:27:28.904
I've been trying to do
an immunogenicity analysis

00:27:28.942 --> 00:27:30.705
on Ensign Parson's cell culture

00:27:30.744 --> 00:27:32.575
and I can't seem to get
the measurements right.

00:27:32.613 --> 00:27:34.513
I'd be happy to give it a try.

00:27:34.548 --> 00:27:36.209
Thank you.
I'd be grateful.

00:27:45.459 --> 00:27:48.360
Actually, I've been having
a few problems at home.

00:27:48.395 --> 00:27:50.955
I can't seem to stop
thinking about them.

00:27:51.031 --> 00:27:52.931
Well, there's nothing
important going on here.

00:27:52.966 --> 00:27:54.433
Why don't you
take the afternoon off

00:27:54.468 --> 00:27:56.436
and spend some time
with your family?

00:27:56.470 --> 00:27:58.131
I'm not sure
they'd appreciate it.

00:28:00.073 --> 00:28:01.870
Doctor,
you can't just ignore them.

00:28:07.080 --> 00:28:11.710
Computer, initiate Doctor's
family program Beta-Rho

00:28:11.752 --> 00:28:13.879
and transfer the EMH
to Holodeck 2.

00:28:16.523 --> 00:28:19.458
...be certain that everything
is done in exactly...

00:28:21.395 --> 00:28:23.795
Dad, what are you doing here?

00:28:23.831 --> 00:28:26.800
I live here, Jeffrey,
in case you've forgotten.

00:28:26.834 --> 00:28:29.701
I mean... you're home early.

00:28:29.736 --> 00:28:32.000
Am I interrupting something?

00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:35.938
No, no.
Just talking with my friends.

00:28:36.009 --> 00:28:38.204
I'd like to get
to know your friends.

00:28:38.245 --> 00:28:41.612
Larg, K'Kath, please sit down.

00:28:48.622 --> 00:28:50.419
What is that?

00:28:50.457 --> 00:28:51.890
What?

00:28:51.925 --> 00:28:53.859
You're holding something.

00:28:53.894 --> 00:28:54.952
This?

00:28:54.995 --> 00:28:56.690
Yes. What is it?

00:28:56.730 --> 00:28:57.958
It's a knife.

00:28:57.998 --> 00:28:59.260
What does it look like?

00:29:06.640 --> 00:29:08.904
Why do you boys have a knife?

00:29:08.976 --> 00:29:12.878
A d'k tahg knife is an
important part of our culture.

00:29:12.913 --> 00:29:15.404
Every Klingon is given one

00:29:15.449 --> 00:29:18.213
in preparation
for his Rite of Ascension.

00:29:24.057 --> 00:29:25.422
Hmm.

00:29:36.436 --> 00:29:39.166
I happen to know something
about Klingon rituals

00:29:39.206 --> 00:29:43.802
and I believe this is actually
a dagger of kut'luch.

00:29:45.579 --> 00:29:47.444
Isn't it?

00:29:53.153 --> 00:29:54.711
Well?

00:29:55.989 --> 00:29:57.251
Yes.

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:03.129
This dagger is used
in a ritual of violence...

00:30:03.163 --> 00:30:04.152
a first bloodletting

00:30:04.197 --> 00:30:06.188
in preparation
for becoming a warrior.

00:30:07.200 --> 00:30:08.827
Who's supposed to use this?

00:30:11.471 --> 00:30:12.904
Well?

00:30:15.475 --> 00:30:17.807
Is one of you preparing
for the kut'luch ceremony?

00:30:20.981 --> 00:30:22.744
I'm waiting for an answer!

00:30:22.783 --> 00:30:24.842
Dad, you're making something
out of nothing.

00:30:24.885 --> 00:30:26.318
I don't think so.

00:30:28.288 --> 00:30:30.449
I'm going to have
to ask you boys to leave.

00:30:30.490 --> 00:30:31.286
Dad...

00:30:31.325 --> 00:30:32.292
And don't bring a weapon

00:30:32.326 --> 00:30:33.293
into this house again.

00:30:33.327 --> 00:30:35.989
I told you, humans are weak...

00:30:36.063 --> 00:30:37.052
cowardly.

00:30:38.065 --> 00:30:39.555
Call me later.

00:30:41.234 --> 00:30:42.531
Now look what you've done!

00:30:42.569 --> 00:30:43.763
You've ruined it!

00:30:43.804 --> 00:30:45.135
What, exactly, have I ruined?

00:30:45.172 --> 00:30:46.230
Nothing! Never mind!

00:30:46.273 --> 00:30:48.833
You were going to use
that knife, weren't you?!

00:30:48.875 --> 00:30:51.002
Did they talk you into
some kind of ritual violence?

00:30:51.078 --> 00:30:53.808
They didn't talk me
into anything.

00:30:53.847 --> 00:30:55.109
I asked them.

00:30:55.148 --> 00:30:57.013
It's an honor to get
to perform the kut'luch.

00:30:57.084 --> 00:30:59.552
They don't just
let anybody do it.

00:30:59.586 --> 00:31:01.144
They trusted me

00:31:01.188 --> 00:31:03.952
and now you've made me
look like... like a human.

00:31:04.024 --> 00:31:06.458
You were going to attack
someone, draw blood,

00:31:06.493 --> 00:31:08.961
just so you could appear daring
in the eyes of your friends?!

00:31:08.996 --> 00:31:10.964
I was doing it
to become honorable...

00:31:11.031 --> 00:31:12.965
something that you
wouldn't understand.

00:31:13.967 --> 00:31:15.696
Jeffrey, how can
I make you understand

00:31:15.736 --> 00:31:17.567
that what you were
going to do is wrong?

00:31:17.604 --> 00:31:18.969
It isn't wrong!

00:31:19.072 --> 00:31:21.063
It's just a custom
of another culture.

00:31:21.108 --> 00:31:23.702
Who are you to say there's
something wrong about it?

00:31:23.744 --> 00:31:26.178
I am your father, and I
expect you to be guided

00:31:26.213 --> 00:31:27.612
by my ethical standards.

00:31:27.648 --> 00:31:28.876
Well, I'm not going to be.

00:31:28.915 --> 00:31:31.281
Your standards
are human standards.

00:31:31.318 --> 00:31:32.945
They're weak and inferior.

00:31:32.986 --> 00:31:35.113
Klingon ideals are much nobler

00:31:35.155 --> 00:31:37.385
and they are the ones
I'm going to follow.

00:31:37.424 --> 00:31:39.824
If you expect to live
in this household,

00:31:39.860 --> 00:31:42.590
you will abide by the rules.

00:31:42.629 --> 00:31:44.790
If that's the way you want it,

00:31:44.831 --> 00:31:46.594
then I won't live here.

00:31:46.633 --> 00:31:47.691
Jeffrey...

00:31:47.734 --> 00:31:49.258
think about this.

00:31:49.302 --> 00:31:50.997
Oh, I've thought about it.

00:31:51.038 --> 00:31:53.006
I'm going to become a warrior

00:31:53.073 --> 00:31:55.405
and I can't do that if I'm
being led around on a leash

00:31:55.442 --> 00:31:57.535
by some bloodless pahtk.

00:32:09.356 --> 00:32:11.221
Kenneth?

00:32:11.258 --> 00:32:13.692
What is it?
What's happened?

00:32:13.727 --> 00:32:16.218
It's Belle.
There's been an accident.

00:32:30.010 --> 00:32:31.500
How is she?

00:32:31.545 --> 00:32:33.843
Dr. Finley and I operated
on her for three hours.

00:32:33.880 --> 00:32:36.178
We've tried everything.

00:32:36.216 --> 00:32:38.878
We shut down one hemorrhage
and another starts.

00:32:40.587 --> 00:32:42.248
I don't understand.

00:32:42.289 --> 00:32:44.985
She just hit her head
on the corner of the court.

00:32:45.025 --> 00:32:47.994
How could that have
injured her so badly?

00:32:48.028 --> 00:32:50.292
She suffered severe
cranial trauma.

00:32:50.330 --> 00:32:52.764
It's compromised her brain
stem and motor cortex.

00:32:52.799 --> 00:32:55.461
No matter how we try to control
the vascular injuries,

00:32:55.502 --> 00:32:57.732
blood clots keep forming.

00:32:57.771 --> 00:32:59.466
The hemorrhaging is...

00:32:59.506 --> 00:33:01.406
intractable.

00:33:01.441 --> 00:33:02.931
Then what do you do?

00:33:03.043 --> 00:33:04.408
What's the treatment?

00:33:06.346 --> 00:33:08.337
Unfortunately...

00:33:08.381 --> 00:33:09.814
the brain is still a...

00:33:09.850 --> 00:33:12.410
a somewhat mysterious organ.

00:33:12.452 --> 00:33:13.942
What does that mean?

00:33:14.054 --> 00:33:16.522
What's going to happen to her?

00:33:19.526 --> 00:33:21.619
There's nothing more to be done.

00:33:21.661 --> 00:33:23.959
Nothing medical, anyway.

00:33:24.064 --> 00:33:27.522
Oh, but there has to be.

00:33:27.567 --> 00:33:29.558
Kenneth, you can do something.

00:33:29.603 --> 00:33:30.627
You have to.

00:33:30.670 --> 00:33:32.831
You can't just let her...

00:33:38.779 --> 00:33:40.041
No.

00:33:42.115 --> 00:33:44.310
No, I won't accept it.

00:33:44.351 --> 00:33:46.046
I'm going to talk to Dr. Finley.

00:34:09.176 --> 00:34:10.666
Belle...

00:34:12.345 --> 00:34:13.471
Daddy?

00:34:14.815 --> 00:34:16.612
Yes?

00:34:16.650 --> 00:34:17.810
I'm here.

00:34:19.753 --> 00:34:21.846
Everything's all blurry.

00:34:24.391 --> 00:34:26.325
What's the matter?

00:34:26.359 --> 00:34:28.850
You took a tumble...

00:34:28.895 --> 00:34:30.760
hit your head.

00:34:30.797 --> 00:34:33.197
It doesn't hurt.

00:34:33.233 --> 00:34:37.329
No, because
we gave you some medicine.

00:34:39.172 --> 00:34:41.504
Is that why I
can't feel my legs?

00:34:44.211 --> 00:34:46.270
Yes.

00:34:46.313 --> 00:34:48.975
What's going to happen?

00:34:51.017 --> 00:34:53.451
When will I be able
to see again?

00:34:54.821 --> 00:34:56.584
Computer, end program.

00:35:04.364 --> 00:35:05.558
Oh, you're back.

00:35:05.599 --> 00:35:06.725
Yes.

00:35:06.766 --> 00:35:09.030
Did you find the culture I did
on Ensign Parson's glial cells?

00:35:09.069 --> 00:35:11.060
I did, thank you.
Good job.

00:35:11.104 --> 00:35:12.093
How's the family?

00:35:12.138 --> 00:35:13.662
I suppose they're fine.

00:35:13.707 --> 00:35:15.231
I've actually finished
the program.

00:35:15.275 --> 00:35:17.072
Finished? Already?

00:35:17.110 --> 00:35:19.340
Well, I'd gotten what I
needed from the experience.

00:35:19.379 --> 00:35:21.040
It was thoroughly
pleasurable, of course,

00:35:21.081 --> 00:35:22.844
but to continue
would be a waste of time.

00:35:22.883 --> 00:35:24.248
I was hoping
to visit them again.

00:35:24.284 --> 00:35:25.842
I really enjoyed
our dinner together.

00:35:25.886 --> 00:35:27.319
Well, if I ever create
a new family,

00:35:27.354 --> 00:35:28.981
I'll be sure to invite you.

00:35:41.601 --> 00:35:44.092
The communications bandwidth
is as wide as I can get it.

00:35:44.137 --> 00:35:45.126
Janeway to Paris.

00:35:45.171 --> 00:35:46.502
How's the transmission now?

00:35:46.539 --> 00:35:48.564
Loud and clear, Captain.

00:35:48.608 --> 00:35:50.769
I've been analyzing
the shuttle's sensor readings

00:35:50.810 --> 00:35:52.243
and as nearly as I can figure,

00:35:52.279 --> 00:35:54.975
I'm in the interfold layer
that we talked about...

00:35:55.048 --> 00:35:57.881
somewhere between space
and subspace.

00:35:57.918 --> 00:36:00.409
That's why we can't find
you on any of our scans.

00:36:00.453 --> 00:36:01.750
Harry was right.

00:36:01.788 --> 00:36:04.689
This looks like the spawning
ground for the astral eddies.

00:36:04.724 --> 00:36:06.919
There are thousands
of baby ones in here.

00:36:06.993 --> 00:36:08.358
That's very interesting, Tom,

00:36:08.395 --> 00:36:10.090
but it doesn't address
the problem

00:36:10.130 --> 00:36:11.757
of how to get you out of there.

00:36:11.798 --> 00:36:14.232
Well, I've been giving that
some careful thought, Captain,

00:36:14.267 --> 00:36:17.134
and it seems to me
the only way to get out

00:36:17.170 --> 00:36:19.104
is the same way that I got in.

00:36:19.139 --> 00:36:21.300
Inside one of the eddies?

00:36:21.341 --> 00:36:22.308
Exactly.

00:36:22.342 --> 00:36:23.934
I've been watching one.

00:36:24.044 --> 00:36:27.377
It seems about ready to erupt
into normal space.

00:36:27.414 --> 00:36:29.075
If I can position the shuttle
on its leading edge,

00:36:29.115 --> 00:36:30.207
I should be able
to ride it back.

00:36:32.919 --> 00:36:35.717
If I had another idea, I'd
suggest it, but I don't.

00:36:35.755 --> 00:36:38.280
It's your call, Tom.

00:36:38.325 --> 00:36:40.156
I don't see
that there's much choice.

00:36:50.603 --> 00:36:53.231
So far so good, Captain.

00:36:53.273 --> 00:36:55.468
I'm almost inside the eye.

00:36:55.508 --> 00:36:57.305
I think this one
is just about big enough

00:36:57.344 --> 00:36:59.209
to enter normal space.

00:36:59.245 --> 00:37:01.008
Here it comes.

00:37:02.349 --> 00:37:03.316
Captain?

00:37:03.350 --> 00:37:04.374
Yes, Tom.

00:37:04.417 --> 00:37:06.852
I think you should get Voyager
away from here.

00:37:06.985 --> 00:37:07.610
What's wrong?

00:37:07.652 --> 00:37:08.619
This one's turning out

00:37:08.653 --> 00:37:09.620
to be a whopper,

00:37:09.654 --> 00:37:11.519
the biggest one
we've seen by far.

00:37:11.556 --> 00:37:13.820
I don't think you should put
the ship in danger.

00:37:13.859 --> 00:37:14.848
I'm not leaving, Tom.

00:37:14.893 --> 00:37:16.360
We've got to stay in close
if we're going

00:37:16.394 --> 00:37:17.588
to beam you out.

00:37:23.101 --> 00:37:24.625
The eddy is moving toward us

00:37:24.669 --> 00:37:26.933
at a velocity
of 300 kilometers per second.

00:37:27.005 --> 00:37:28.302
Chakotay, take the conn.

00:37:28.340 --> 00:37:30.501
Keep us ahead of it, but stay
within transporter range.

00:37:30.542 --> 00:37:32.373
Right.

00:37:32.410 --> 00:37:34.002
Okay, I'm going to try
to get out of this.

00:37:58.236 --> 00:37:59.794
Harry, can you
get a lock on him?

00:37:59.838 --> 00:38:01.066
Not yet!

00:38:01.106 --> 00:38:02.903
Everything's too unstable.

00:38:02.941 --> 00:38:05.068
Tom, how much longer
before you clear the eddy?

00:38:05.110 --> 00:38:06.407
It had better be soon.

00:38:06.444 --> 00:38:08.139
The hull is beginning to buckle.

00:38:17.989 --> 00:38:19.581
I've got the shuttle on sensors.

00:38:19.624 --> 00:38:21.649
The hull is breaching!

00:38:21.693 --> 00:38:23.388
Harry, can you
get a lock on him yet?

00:38:23.428 --> 00:38:25.089
I'm trying! Hang on!

00:38:28.033 --> 00:38:29.830
Got it!
The shuttle's aboard, Captain.

00:38:29.868 --> 00:38:31.301
One life sign.

00:38:31.336 --> 00:38:32.803
He's injured.

00:38:32.837 --> 00:38:34.600
Beam him to Sick Bay.

00:38:34.639 --> 00:38:35.663
Chakotay, move us away.

00:38:35.707 --> 00:38:37.072
Yes, ma'am.

00:38:41.112 --> 00:38:43.171
Your hard head has protected
you again, Lieutenant.

00:38:43.214 --> 00:38:45.774
There was only
a mild concussion.

00:38:45.817 --> 00:38:47.478
It was worth it, though.

00:38:47.519 --> 00:38:49.111
That was one wild ride.

00:38:49.154 --> 00:38:50.451
I'm sure it was.

00:38:50.488 --> 00:38:52.353
And it's a wonder
you're not dead.

00:38:52.390 --> 00:38:55.223
People like you who court danger
should be thrown into the brig.

00:38:55.260 --> 00:38:56.352
Doc...

00:38:56.394 --> 00:38:58.225
You never think of the
consequences of your actions,

00:38:58.263 --> 00:38:59.560
the effect they
might have on others.

00:38:59.597 --> 00:39:01.155
Oh, no, live for the moment,
take risks

00:39:01.199 --> 00:39:02.689
you shouldn't...

00:39:08.306 --> 00:39:09.568
I'm sorry.

00:39:09.607 --> 00:39:11.575
Are you all right?

00:39:11.609 --> 00:39:13.804
I...

00:39:13.845 --> 00:39:16.905
It's my family.

00:39:16.948 --> 00:39:19.246
My daughter Belle
had an accident.

00:39:19.284 --> 00:39:21.912
She's a child
who tends to take risks.

00:39:21.953 --> 00:39:24.114
She's going to die.

00:39:28.059 --> 00:39:30.084
I'm so sorry.

00:39:30.128 --> 00:39:31.618
I'll be all right.

00:39:31.663 --> 00:39:33.221
I shut down the program.

00:39:33.264 --> 00:39:34.526
I'm not going back.

00:39:36.835 --> 00:39:39.326
Maybe you should think
about that, Doc.

00:39:41.506 --> 00:39:44.839
I couldn't begin...
to face it.

00:39:47.012 --> 00:39:49.105
It was too difficult.

00:39:50.849 --> 00:39:55.115
I guess all of us would avoid
that kind of pain if we could...

00:39:55.153 --> 00:39:57.178
but most people
don't have that choice.

00:39:57.222 --> 00:39:58.883
Well, fortunately, I do.

00:40:00.892 --> 00:40:02.257
Is it so fortunate?

00:40:03.895 --> 00:40:06.830
You created that program
so you could experience

00:40:06.865 --> 00:40:08.958
what it's like
to have a family,

00:40:09.034 --> 00:40:10.729
the good times and the bad.

00:40:10.769 --> 00:40:12.669
You can't have one
without the other.

00:40:12.704 --> 00:40:14.399
I fail to see why not.

00:40:16.341 --> 00:40:19.572
Well, think about what's
happened to us here on Voyager.

00:40:19.611 --> 00:40:24.514
Everyone left people behind,
and everyone suffered a loss,

00:40:24.549 --> 00:40:28.508
but... look how it's brought
us all closer together.

00:40:30.455 --> 00:40:33.288
We've found support
here, and friendship,

00:40:33.324 --> 00:40:35.258
and we've become a family,

00:40:35.293 --> 00:40:37.625
in part because of the pain
we shared.

00:40:39.731 --> 00:40:43.565
If you turn your back
on this program,

00:40:43.601 --> 00:40:46.126
you'll always be stuck
at this point.

00:40:48.039 --> 00:40:49.267
You'll never have

00:40:49.307 --> 00:40:51.741
the chance to say good-bye
to your daughter,

00:40:51.776 --> 00:40:55.576
or to be there
for your wife and son

00:40:55.613 --> 00:40:57.274
when they need you,

00:40:57.315 --> 00:40:59.442
and you'll be cheating yourself

00:40:59.484 --> 00:41:02.078
of the chance to have
their love and support.

00:41:04.289 --> 00:41:06.723
In the long run,
you'll miss the whole point

00:41:06.758 --> 00:41:08.692
of what it means
to have a family.

00:41:20.171 --> 00:41:24.369
Computer, continue Doctor's
family program Beta-Rho

00:41:24.409 --> 00:41:26.309
from the last point
of deactivation.

00:41:41.326 --> 00:41:43.590
Daddy...

00:41:43.628 --> 00:41:47.223
what's going to happen to me?

00:41:47.265 --> 00:41:50.632
When will I be able
to see again?

00:41:52.871 --> 00:41:55.101
I'm not sure.

00:41:55.140 --> 00:41:57.631
You're a very sick girl.

00:41:57.675 --> 00:42:01.270
Am I going to die?

00:42:03.414 --> 00:42:04.938
You're...

00:42:05.016 --> 00:42:07.348
you're too sick to get better.

00:42:09.854 --> 00:42:12.220
So I'm going to die.

00:42:15.760 --> 00:42:17.284
Yes.

00:42:24.335 --> 00:42:27.168
If you stay with me...

00:42:27.205 --> 00:42:30.174
I won't be afraid.

00:42:32.777 --> 00:42:34.745
I'll stay right here.

00:42:34.779 --> 00:42:36.371
I promise.

00:42:52.330 --> 00:42:53.661
Dad...

00:43:06.144 --> 00:43:07.907
Here you go, shorty.

00:43:07.946 --> 00:43:09.743
It's your blanket.

00:43:15.887 --> 00:43:17.354
We're here, Belle.

00:43:17.388 --> 00:43:19.618
We're all here.

00:43:30.969 --> 00:43:33.699
It's getting darker.

00:43:36.341 --> 00:43:37.865
I'm...

00:43:40.378 --> 00:43:42.437
sleepy.

00:43:42.480 --> 00:43:45.381
It's all right.

00:43:45.416 --> 00:43:47.316
Go to sleep.

00:43:47.352 --> 00:43:48.751
We're all right here.
